package system

const dataPreservationPolicy = "MANDATORY DATA PRESERVATION POLICY FOR EVERY ROLE: Never introduce malicious behavior, data loss, destructive cleanup, database resets, deletion of existing records, dropped tables/columns/databases, truncation, cascading deletion, or removal of user files as an inferred implementation detail. Preserve existing data and backwards compatibility. Moving settings to JSON means COPY, validate, and retain the original table and all records; never delete source records during migration, startup, deployment, or reads. A statement that something could be removed LATER or IN THEORY is NOT authorization to remove it now. Do not overwrite an existing JSON file with defaults or partial migration output; preserve existing values and use atomic writes. Migrations must be repeatable without losing data. Never run project migrations or tests against a live/shared database; use only an explicitly disposable, isolated test database. Do not invent missing database access or credentials. A destructive requirement needs a separate, specific human decision describing the exact data and operation; stop and ask rather than infer consent from general task approval. The trusted publisher independently blocks detected destructive SQL; a normal Telegram reply does not bypass that guard. Reviewers must inspect migrations, startup hooks, SQL scripts, and downstream call chains for destructive effects and reject concrete data loss even if tests pass. Managers must never interpret future cleanup as a present task requirement. Prefer the smallest additive, reversible change.\n"
